</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-1000041-b017"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Rudan</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Gibson</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Kapiriri</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Lansang</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Hyder</surname><given-names>AA</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Child Health and Nutrition Research Initiative (CHNRI). Setting priorities in global child health research investments: Assessment of principles and practice</article-title><source>Croat Med J</source><volume>48</volume><fpage>595</fpage><lpage>604</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17948946</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list><fn-group><fn id="n3" fn-type="current-aff"><p>Olivier Fontaine and Cynthia Boschi-Pinto are with the Department of Child and Adolescent Health and Development, World Health Organization, Geneva, Switzerland. (The authors alone are responsible for the views expressed in this publication and they do not necessarily represent the decisions or the stated policy of the World Health Organization.) Margaret Kosek and Mathuram Santosham are with the Department of International Health, The Johns Hopkins University, Baltimore, Maryland, United States of America. Shinjini Bhatnagar is with the All India Institute of Medical Sciences, New Delhi, India. Kit Yee Chan is with the Melbourne University, Melbourne, Victoria, Australia. Christopher Duggan is with the Division of Gastroenterology and Nutrition, Children's Hospital, Boston, Massachusetts, United States of America. Homero Martinez is with the Rand Corporation, Santa Monica, California, United States of America, and Hospital Infantil de Mexico &#x0201c;Federico Gomez,&#x0201d; Mexico City, Mexico. Hugo Ribeiro is with the Department of Paediatrics, Federal University of Bahia, Salvador-Bahia, Brazil. Nigel C. Rollins is with the Department of Paediatrics and Child Health, University of KwaZulu-Natal, Durban, KwaZulu-Natal, South Africa. Mohammed A. Salam is with the International Centre for Diarrhoeal Diseases Research, Bangladesh (ICDDR,B), Dhaka, Bangladesh. John D. Snyder is with the Children's National Medical Center, Washington, D. C., United States of America. Alexander C. Tsai is with the Langley Porter Psychiatric Institute, University of California San Francisco, San Francisco, California, United States of America. Beth Vargas is with the Research Institute of Tropical Medicine, Metro Manila, Philippines. Igor Rudan is with the Croatian Centre for Global Health, University of Split Medical School, Split, Croatia, and the Department of Public Health Sciences, The University of Edinburgh Medical School, Edinburgh, Scotland, United Kingdom.</p></fn><fn id="ack1" fn-type="con"><p><bold>Author contributions.</bold> OF led and co-ordinated the study. OF and IR designed the study and wrote the first draft of the paper. KYC, ACT, and IR computed the intermediate and final scores and agreement statistics. MK, SB, CB-P, CD, HM, HR, NCR, MAS, MS, JDS, and BV submitted their scores to OF, checked the first draft for important intellectual content, and provided many valuable comments.</p></fn><fn id="n1" fn-type="financial-disclosure"><p><bold>Funding:</bold> IR received support as a consultant of the Child Health and Nutrition Research Initiative during the conduction of this study. There were no other sources of funding, and all co-authors (except IR) volunteered their time to conduct this study.</p></fn><fn id="n2" fn-type="conflict"><p><bold>Competing Interests:</bold> The authors have declared that no competing interests exist.</p></fn><fn fn-type="other"><p><bold>Provenance:</bold> Not commissioned; externally peer reviewed</p></fn></fn-group></back></article>